"network."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Security/Introducing-ros2-security.rst:365
msgid "Take the Quiz!"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Security/Introducing-ros2-security.rst:369
msgid "Question 1"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Security/Introducing-ros2-security.rst:371
msgid ""
"Open another terminal session, but **do not** set the environment variables "
"so that security is not enabled. Start the listener. What do you expect to "
"happen?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Security/Introducing-ros2-security.rst:375
msgid "Answer 1"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Security/Introducing-ros2-security.rst:377
msgid ""
"The listener launches but does not receive any messages. All traffic is "
"encrypted, and without security enabled the listener does not receive "
"anything."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Security/Introducing-ros2-security.rst:383
msgid "Question 2"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Security/Introducing-ros2-security.rst:385
msgid ""
"Stop the listener, set the environment variable ``ROS_SECURITY_ENABLE`` to "
"``true`` and start the listener again. What results do you expect this time?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Security/Introducing-ros2-security.rst:388
msgid "Answer 2"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Security/Introducing-ros2-security.rst:390
msgid ""
"The listener still launches but does not receive messages. Although security "
"has now been enabled, it is not been configured properly since ROS is unable "
"to locate the key files. The listener launches, but in non-secure mode since "
"security is not enforced, which means that although the properly configured "
"talker is sending encrypted messages, this listener is unable to decrypt "
"them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Security/Introducing-ros2-security.rst:396
msgid "Question 3"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Security/Introducing-ros2-security.rst:398
msgid ""
"Stop the listener and set ``ROS_SECURITY_STRATEGY`` to ``Enforce``. What "
"happens now?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Security/Introducing-ros2-security.rst:401
msgid "Answer 3"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Security/Introducing-ros2-security.rst:403
msgid ""
"The listener fails to launch. Security has been enabled and is being "
"enforced. Since it still is not properly configured, an error is thrown "
"rather than launching in non-secure mode."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Security/Introducing-ros2-security.rst:409
msgid "Learn More!"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Security/Introducing-ros2-security.rst:411
msgid ""
"Are you ready to go further with ROS Security? Take a look at the `Secure "
"Turtlebot2 Demo <https://github.com/ros-swg/turtlebot3_demo>`_. You'll find "
"a functioning and complex implementation of ROS 2 security, ready to try out "
"your own custom scenarios. Be sure to create pull requests and issues here "
"so we can continue improving security support in ROS!"
msgstr ""
